## 12. MONTHLY SALES TARGET AND BONUS SYSTEM

Administrators must be able to configure monthly sales targets and bonuses.

Example:
- Monthly sales target: ৳100,000.
- Bonus for achieving the target: ৳800.

The target is based on the total accepted selling value of eligible delivered orders attributed to the affiliate during the applicable calendar month, subject to the platform's configured adjustment policy.

### Essential rules

- Pending orders do not count.
- Confirmed orders do not count.
- Processing orders do not count.
- Shipped orders do not count.
- Only delivered orders qualify.
- Cancelled orders do not count.
- Returned orders must be adjusted according to the configured return policy.
- Do not count the same order more than once.
- Use the configured Bangladesh business timezone for monthly boundaries.

For each affiliate, display:
- Monthly target.
- Eligible delivered sales.
- Percentage completed.
- Remaining sales required.
- Bonus amount.
- Bonus eligibility status.
- Bonus payment status.

Example:

| Eligible monthly sales | Progress | Bonus |
|---|---:|---:|
| ৳25,000 | 25% | ৳0 |
| ৳50,000 | 50% | ৳0 |
| ৳75,000 | 75% | ৳0 |
| ৳100,000 | 100% | ৳800 |

The example assumes a single ৳800 bonus for reaching the target.

Do not issue the same monthly bonus repeatedly because of duplicate events or repeated status updates.

Use an auditable monthly bonus record.

### Admin controls

Allow the administrator to:
- Set a default monthly target.
- Set the bonus amount.
- Configure individual affiliate targets if required.
- View progress for every affiliate.
- Filter by month and affiliate.
- Review bonus eligibility.
- Record bonus payment status.

Design the system so additional target tiers can be introduced later without rebuilding the entire application.

