## 18. SECURITY RULES AND SERVER-SIDE VALIDATION

Security is a mandatory part of the implementation.

Create Firestore Security Rules and Firebase Cloud Functions.

Implement the principle of least privilege.

### Required security behavior

- Only authorized administrators can manage platform-wide products, orders, settings, affiliate approvals, and payouts.
- Affiliates can read and update only permitted fields of their own profiles.
- Affiliates cannot approve themselves.
- Affiliates cannot assign themselves an admin role.
- Affiliates cannot modify their own commission records.
- Affiliates cannot modify payout status.
- Affiliates cannot edit platform-wide pricing rules.
- Customers cannot read arbitrary customer records.
- Customers cannot modify order totals or affiliate commissions.
- All sensitive financial calculations are performed or validated on the server.
- Public access to private Firestore collections must be denied.
- Admin operations must be authorized server-side.
- Firebase Admin SDK credentials and service account secrets must never be exposed in the browser.

Use Firebase Authentication, custom claims where appropriate, server-side validation, and Firestore Security Rules together.

Never rely on hidden buttons or frontend route guards as the only security mechanism.

Generate secure, auditable status transitions.

Provide clear instructions for deploying the Security Rules and Cloud Functions.

Do not use open Firestore rules such as unrestricted public reads or writes.

